refined_feedback:
The division by `n` should be performed before checking if `i` is a divisor, to avoid potential division-by-zero errors. 

```c
bool my_prime(int n) {
    if (n <= 1) return false;
    for (int i = 2; i * i <= n; i++) {
        if (n % i == 0) return false;
    }
    return true;
}
```

Alternatively, you can start checking from `sqrt(n)` instead of `i` to further optimize the function.

```c
bool my_prime(int n) {
    if (n <= 1) return false;
    for (int i = 2; i * i <= n; i++) {
        if (n % i == 0) return false;
    }
    return true;
}
```
Conceptual principle: When checking for divisibility, it's more efficient to check divisors up to the square root of the number instead of all possible numbers.

