conceptual_feedback:
Here's the simplified code:

```c
double power(double x) {
    double result = 1;
    double current = x;

    while (current <= sqrt(current)) {
        result *= current;
        current *= x;
    }

    return result;
}
```

This function uses a `while` loop to iteratively calculate the square of `x`, effectively computing `x^2`. The loop continues until `current` is greater than its own square root, at which point `result` has been multiplied by all necessary powers of `x`.

