refined_feedback:
The current implementation increments the input value instead of checking numbers greater than it to find the next prime number. 

Corrected Code:
```c
int is_prime(int num) {
    if (num <= 1) return 0;
    for (int i = 2; i * i <= num; i++) {
        if (num % i == 0) return 0;
    }
    return 1;
}

int next_prime(int n) {
    int num = n + 1;
    while (!is_prime(num)) {
        num++;
    }
    return num;
}
```
This corrected version checks numbers greater than `n` to find the first prime number in sequence.

