**Optimized Prime Check**

To improve efficiency in checking if a number is prime, iterate only up to the square root of `nb`.

```c
int is_prime(int nb) {
    int sqrt_nb = (int)sqrt(nb);
    for (int i = 2; i <= sqrt_nb; i++) {
        if (nb % i == 0) {
            return 0; // not prime
        }
    }
    return 1; // prime
}
```

**Rationale**

Checking divisibility up to the square root of `nb` is more efficient than checking all the way to `nb`, as any factor larger than the square root would have a corresponding factor smaller than the square root.

