conceptual_feedback:
**Optimizing a Loop with Square Root**

The suggestion proposes using the square root function (`sqrt`) to improve the performance of the loop by reducing the number of iterations.

**Key Concept:** Use the square root function as the upper limit of the loop condition, rather than squaring the current iteration value (`i * i`).

Example Code:
```c
int sqrt(int nb) {
    int low = 0;
    int high = nb;

    while (low <= high) {
        int mid = low + (high - low) / 2;
        if (mid * mid == nb)
            return mid;
        else if (mid * mid > nb)
            high = mid - 1;
        else
            low = mid + 1;
    }
    return -1; // not found
}

int optimizedLoop(int nb) {
    int i = 0;
    while (i * i <= nb)
        i++;
    return i;
}
```
This optimization technique can significantly improve the performance of loops that iterate over a range, especially when dealing with large values.

